--- a/README.md
+++ b/README.md
@@ -74,6 +74,7 @@ original. Anything that cannot be derived from the b1.7.3 sources is marked
 | Stamina (Stamina port) | written without a full toolchain: type-checked and `stamina::tests::*` (5) + `vitals::tests::damage_like_java` run in a Linux scratch crate; the HUD and `lib.rs` wiring not run on a device | `world/stamina.rs`: insane96mcp's Stamina (NeoForge 26.1.2), read from its sources, its default numbers. 200 stamina (10 per health point, armor -2.5% a point); a sprint costs 1 a tick (x0.8 out of combat, 15 s after a hit dealt or taken), a jump 10; empty = locked: no sprinting until it regenerates (2 a tick, x0.6 while locked) to 40%; at 20% health the bar is emptied and locked; locked walks x0.9, sprinting under 40 / 20% x0.85 more. HUD: grey half-heart overlay on the hearts it no longer covers (darker while locked), `Stamina` row in the debug screen. Not ported: Vigour / Curse of Weariness, the Vigour effect, swimming, mining cost, hunger spend, the command, the sync, the config. See the gameplay changelog. |
 | Biome atmosphere (2026-10-24) | written without a toolchain: not compiled, not run (+6 tests: 5 in `world/atmos.rs`, 1 in `world/sky.rs`) | `world/atmos.rs`: every biome (19) has its own sky top / horizon-fog colours, haze band, exp² terrain fog density, cloud tint / cover / speed and star tint / brightness; 9 columns around the player are averaged (so a border is felt 48 blocks early) and the frame's values ease toward that with a 2 s time constant in real seconds. The vanilla day / rain / thunder curves still run, scaled by `biome noon colour / vanilla noon colour`, so night stays dark in every biome. Clouds are b1.7.3's fancy clouds (12-block cells, 4 thick, y 108, drifting along +x) ray-marched per sky pixel in the dome shader (WGSL + GLSL, no geometry), with sides and undersides shaded and melting into the fog. See the rendering changelog. |
 | Atmosphere editor (2026-10-24) | written without a toolchain: not compiled, not run (+2 tests in `world/atmos.rs`, +1 in `options.rs`) | Pause menu > the pixel sun at its bottom right corner (not on the death screen). A panel down the left; the world stays undimmed beside it and follows every slider at once. `<` name `>` or the list picks the biome (opens on the one under the player, a gold dot marks edited ones); tabs Sky / Fog / Clouds / Haze / Stars hold all 21 values of `world::atmos`'s look (colour as red / green / blue sliders with a swatch and hex code, plus gradient, fog density, cloud cover and speed, haze strength, star brightness). `Reset biome` / `Reset all`. Edited biomes are saved as `atmos_<n>:` lines of options.txt (n = the biome's place in `atmos::ALL`) when a slider is let go. Colours are the biome's noon colours: night and rain still follow the vanilla curves. Not there: a time-of-day / weather preview, copy and paste of a look, an in-world list of the biome under the cursor. |
+| Biome rules + wolf (2026-10-27) | compiled for aarch64-linux-android; the tests of the touched modules run on a Linux host; **NOT seen or heard on a device**; NOT b1.7.3 | `world/biomelife.rs` (`biomeRules` in options.txt, on): fog shortens mob sight, heat and cold weigh on stamina, seasons tint the two forests and set the apples, leaves give apples; `animalAi`: wolves hunt sheep and sheep graze the grass. The wolf is Acidul's Wolves (`render/wolf_model.rs`, `assets/wolf.rgba`, `tools/gen_wolf.py`) in six coats by biome, with seven voices (`assets/sound/wolf/`). Numbers and the export table in `roadmap/design.md` |
 | Shoulder-surf view (2026-10-24) | written without a toolchain: not compiled, not run, not seen on a device (+8 tests in `render/shoulder.rs`, the view-button test rewritten in `touch_ui.rs`); `python3 tools/shoulder_proto.py` (the twin of the maths) passes | `render/shoulder.rs`: a cinematic over-the-shoulder camera, the view button's second tap (first person -> third -> shoulder surf). NOT b1.7.3. Glides in from the vanilla third-person place (4 blocks behind the eye, no dolly out from the head, no field-of-view whip), a pivot a shoulder to the right that follows through springs (slower on xz than y), crosshair convergence (the camera turns to the point the eye's pick ray hits, rack-focused), automatic shoulder swap at a wall, 5-ray collision (instant in, eased out), bank into strafes and turns, landing dip / jump lift / hit kick on under-damped springs, sneak tuck, zoom = aiming shot, sprint pull-back, hand-held sway. See the rendering changelog. |
 | Grazing + idle behaviours (2026-10-25) | written without a toolchain: not compiled, not run; **NOT b1.7.3** (+4 tests in `world/mobs.rs`, +1 in `render/items.rs`; run `cargo test --lib mobs items` first) | Part of the smart animals switch (`animalAi`, on by default; `animalAi:false` gives the b1.7.3 AI back byte for byte). `Mob::idle`: a calm pig, cow, sheep or hen pauses to do something instead of only standing: a cow or sheep on grass **grazes** (3 to 8 s), a pig **roots** on grass or dirt (2 to 5 s), a hen **pecks** (1 to 2 s), and a cow, sheep or pig now and then **rests** (8 to 20 s). Eating and resting stay put, do not turn, and end when a person comes within 4 blocks or the animal is hit. Each wander walk has its own gait (a stroll at 0.6 to 1.0 x the walk, a hen sometimes dashes at 1.5 x). The head is drawn dipped to the ground (`Mob::head`, `Mob::munch`, `render/items.rs::head_dip`) with a chew or a quick peck. The grass is not eaten and nothing lies down. See the gameplay changelog. |
 | Immersive pack (The Forest style, 2026-10-25) | written without a toolchain: not compiled, not run, not seen on a device (+5 tests in `world/pack.rs`, `menu.rs` flow test extended, carry check in `render/player.rs`); **NOT b1.7.3** | `world/pack.rs` + `lib.rs` + `render/items.rs` + `menu.rs`: with the world's **Immersive Pack** switch on (Create World screen, saved as the 4th line of `<world>/info`; worlds made before it keep the panel), the inventory button no longer opens the inventory: the player takes the pack in both hands (it rises from below, the held item is hidden) and the cloth shows on the flat ground under the crosshair, lime where it fits and red where it does not (needs a full block under 9 samples of a 2.0 x 1.6 footprint, nothing but air or plants on it); a tap, like placing a block, spreads it there (on a red one only a message shows), the button again puts the pack away. The cloth unrolls in the world (0.9 s, a roll that shrinks as it travels), then the screen opens as the cloth: items lie in zones by category (tools & gear, food, materials, other), each at its own size, shrunk together when a zone is crowded; the crafting mat (2 x 2), worn armor and the quick-select row (hotbar) have fixed places. Same `SlotId`s and `Screen::click` as the panel, so crafting, armor, spread-drag, place-one and shift-click work unchanged. Closing, walking 6.5 blocks off or losing the ground rolls it up. A workbench, furnace and chest keep their own panels. Switch off = the old panel. See the gameplay changelog. **Update 2026-10-25 (12):** the screen is a fixed table (main cloth, a small crafting cloth in front, an armor stand at its right, the quick-select belt) that the camera pans over by dragging on empty cloth or ground; four 3D tabs (Pack, Crafting, Armor, Quick) jump the view to a part, four 3D buttons (close, shift-click, place one, sort) lie at its edges, and the four HUD buttons, the two blue toggles and the `Quick select` text are gone. See the gameplay changelog. |
